WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.590
The fourth and final part of Netflix's Sabrina
is a veritable Pandora's box of Eldritch terrors

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:11.320
and OG aunties with an intensely emotional
ending that will have many fans wishing for

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.320
another season.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.740
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm breaking down the series finale

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.650
of CAOS,
clues and theories about what would have happened

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.720
in the now-cancelled Part 5, and whether Sabrina
could still return.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.339
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:26.339 --> 00:00:30.849
The main events of the finale kick off when
Sabrina Morningstar crashes through the magic

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:33.510
mirror as she returns from the duplicate cosmos.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:38.129
Having fled the alternate Earth with a talking
Salem who's actually an Eldritch terror himself,

00:00:38.129 --> 00:00:42.489
she arrives back in Sabrina Spellman's bedroom
and warns her that the Void is on its way

00:00:42.489 --> 00:00:44.109
to destroy the Earth.

00:00:44.109 --> 00:00:48.570
But Morningstar's escape and journey between
the two worlds has left her badly injured

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.420
and she and Salem quickly die.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:55.789
In an effort to stop the Void, Sabrina Spellman
is about to make a wish on the reality-altering

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:59.929
Imp of the Perverse when the mysterious trinket
salesman shows up.

00:00:59.929 --> 00:01:04.040
Sabrina trades the Imp for Pandora's Box,
the mythical object said to have unleashed

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.450
evil and terror into the world.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:10.550
Sabrina using Pandora's fabled box against
the Eldritch terrors which Blackwood summoned

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:15.550
is a nice call-back to Part 2 when she taunted
him about her newfound powers to resurrect

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:16.810
and perform miracles.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:21.140
"The gods give Pandora a jar containing all
the sorrows of the world.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:24.340
They armed her for vengeance, Father Blackwood.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:25.340
For destruction.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.590
Do you really want to open that lid?"

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:31.410
Sabrina then ventures into the Void alone
and, as she wants to take full responsibility

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:36.180
for the impending apocalypse, she blocks off
the magic mirror so no one can follow her.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.620
Given that the Void by definition represents
nothingness, the design the CAOS team came

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.970
up with is interesting.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:45.600
The pictures in the room are by the renowned
Dutch graphic artist M.C.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.420
Escher who was known for his depictions of
mathematical and impossible objects.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:55.040
For example, when you look at this pair-of-hands
drawing, the image creates a strange illusionary

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.490
loop in your mind so you can't tell where
the picture begins or ends.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:02.290
And it seems like a fitting choice perhaps
given that it was Sabrina's refusal to go

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:06.700
back and complete the time loop at the end
of Part 3 which led to this situation in the

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.700
first place.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.850
"When you're done with everything you have
to come back to right here, right now, and

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:14.340
do what I just did to complete the time loop.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.810
It's the only way to keep the realms preserved."

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:21.310
Another intriguing piece of Escher's art in
the Void is "Day and Night", with its symmetrical

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:26.280
mirroring of dark and light birds flying in
opposite directions that merge into a patchwork

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.140
of tiled fields below.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:33.280
This piece seems to perfectly represent Sabrina's
dual nature with her mortal and infernal sides

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.420
as well as the merging of the two different
but same Sabrinas this season.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:41.630
Now that she's in the Void, Sabrina opens
up Pandora's Box which starts sucking the

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:43.630
final Eldritch terror into it.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:48.290
But this time it's not her impetuousness that
messes up the plan as it's often done in the

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:51.100
past;
instead, back on Earth, her aunties, Ambrose

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:55.940
and Nick have cast a spell that brings Spellman's
soul back into Morningstar's dead body.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:59.990
And although the Void appears to have been
defeated when they discover it's disappeared

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:04.240
from the Academy's Observatory, weird things
begin to happen the next day.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:09.240
It's Sabrina's 17th birthday, one year on
from the events of the first season, and objects

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.650
and even people start to mysteriously disappear
around her.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:17.301
A scan reveals that Sabrina's insides appear
empty and they realise that the Void is now

00:03:17.301 --> 00:03:19.190
inside her.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:22.990
Understanding that she's a threat to everyone
and everything around her, Sabrina selflessly

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:26.790
banishes herself to the Mountains of Madness
to protect those she loves.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:31.710
Blackwood, who knows the Void's arrived, seeks
out Sabrina with the intention of sacrificing

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:36.380
her by draining out the Eldritch terror,
then containing it and consuming it to obtain

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:40.160
its powers, similar to when he ate a piece
of the Uninvited.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.490
Team Spellman goes to the Mountains of Madness
for a final showdown with Blackwood and the

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:49.160
Void, during which Faustus is neutralised
after they trick him with a fake Pandora's

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.950
Box, blinding him with gunpowder.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:54.959
However, Sabrina, who's been learning everything
about the Void, explains that Blackwood's

00:03:54.959 --> 00:03:59.470
plan to blood-let her is still the only way
to extract the Eldritch terror from inside

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:00.470
her.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.209
And although she and her aunties fear the
worst, she shows strength, leadership and

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:06.120
bravery in her final moments.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:09.470
"The Void believes in nothing, thinks we don't
matter.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:10.470
But we do.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:13.569
We have a strength and a bond that the Void
can't touch.

00:04:13.569 --> 00:04:16.199
So let's finish this the way we always do...
together."

00:04:16.199 --> 00:04:22.019
It's a very emotional moment given the risks
and even a little Iron Man Endgame-esque.

00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:25.759
And just before they begin, there's a little
bit of foreshadowing of how Nick will end

00:04:25.759 --> 00:04:27.590
up joining Sabrina in the afterlife.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:29.289
"I'll see you on the other side."

00:04:29.289 --> 00:04:34.270
As the white Void flows out of Sabrina, she
tries to hold on but it just takes too long,

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:39.000
and in her final moments she says goodbye
to everyone as a montage flashes past.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.259
It's a heart-breaking time for Nick especially
when he emerges last from the Void to tell

00:04:43.259 --> 00:04:47.100
Sabrina they saved everyone, only to learn
she's dead.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.660
Nick and Sabrina, of course, do end up together
in the very final scene of the series as he

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:55.860
joins her in the "The Sweet Hereafter", revealing
that he went swimming in the Sea of Sorrows

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.020
and drowned.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:00.461
Whether he meant that literally or figuratively,
it seems that Nick was determined to be with

00:05:00.461 --> 00:05:03.259
Sabrina and decided to join her in the afterlife.

00:05:03.259 --> 00:05:05.530
"Sabrina Spellman...
we're end-game."

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:10.050
That's similar to what Sabrina told Harvey
in Part 3 about him and Roz who also end up

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:11.620
together by the end of the series.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.930
"You guys are endgame."

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:17.380
A couple of interesting details are that Sabrina
now has a white headband rather than the black

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.469
or red ones we've seen her with.

00:05:19.469 --> 00:05:23.629
And as Nick and Sabrina kiss, he pulls her
hand to the chain around his neck that holds

00:05:23.629 --> 00:05:27.180
his locket, the other one of which he gave
her for her 17th birthday.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.000
"One for me...
and one for you.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.159
So that I'll always be able to find you."

00:05:31.159 --> 00:05:35.610
A few other moments foreshadowing this scene
include when Nick told Sabrina that he wanted

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.139
to be a part of her world.

00:05:37.139 --> 00:05:38.710
"Calm down Ariel."

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:43.059
And also as Sabrina is dying you can hear
a little echo of her telling Nick

00:05:43.059 --> 00:05:44.629
"I'm never letting you go."

00:05:44.629 --> 00:05:49.180
That's something Sabrina said to Nick in Part
3 after he returned to her from being trapped

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:50.560
with Lucifer in the Acheron.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.129
"I'm never letting you go."

00:05:52.129 --> 00:05:56.101
And although I have mixed feelings about this
final scene and how the series ended, it's

00:05:56.101 --> 00:06:01.229
worth noting that Sabrina looks happy and
at peace with herself even before Nick arrives.

00:06:01.229 --> 00:06:05.210
That's because Sabrina learning to love herself
was a big theme in Part 4.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:08.210
"We will always be loved.

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:10.819
We have each other, and we love each other."

00:06:10.819 --> 00:06:15.339
Then there was that great moment when the
two Sabrinas just hung out and had fun dancing

00:06:15.339 --> 00:06:16.400
with each other.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:20.289
We also see how Sabrina comes to understand
that although she can have a boyfriend if

00:06:20.289 --> 00:06:23.599
she chooses, she doesn't absolutely need one
to be happy.

00:06:23.599 --> 00:06:25.240
"Who needs boys when we have each other?"

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:29.759
Amusingly though, Spellman does have a go
at making her own ideal man by using the candle

00:06:29.759 --> 00:06:32.569
she inscribed with Nick and Harvey's names
in Part 3.

00:06:32.569 --> 00:06:35.650
"May you be the best of both Nick and Harvey."

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:40.089
And although things don't exactly work out
with Lucas Hunt, Sabrina quickly moves on

00:06:40.089 --> 00:06:43.449
from the brief fling and flushes the wax man
down the drain.

00:06:43.449 --> 00:06:44.449
"Boys.

00:06:44.449 --> 00:06:46.319
I think I need to be alone for a little while.

00:06:46.319 --> 00:06:48.879
I need to figure out who I am."

00:06:48.879 --> 00:06:52.160
It's great to see Sabrina maturing in this
way in her final season

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.979
as it's been something of an intentional running
joke through the series about how she often

00:06:55.979 --> 00:07:00.300
ploughs ahead doing exactly the opposite of
what everyone else is recommending.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:04.210
This criticism has been a little unfair at
times, given she's only young and will naturally

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:09.149
want to do her own thing, and be curious,
rebellious, and even foolhardy at times.

00:07:09.149 --> 00:07:13.350
And despite a few stumbles such as getting
drunk and causing a scene at Hilda's wedding,

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:18.129
by the time the Eldritch terror the Cosmic
arrives on the horizon, Sabrina and her doppelganger

00:07:18.129 --> 00:07:21.259
decide to step up to the plate and take full
accountability.

00:07:21.259 --> 00:07:22.589
"This mess is our fault.

00:07:22.589 --> 00:07:26.300
We won't be responsible for countless deaths
of witches, mortals, and infernals."

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:30.949
The idea that Sabrina's reckless decisions
would culminate in a grand reckoning was mentioned

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:33.389
way back in Part 2 by her aunt Hilda.

00:07:33.389 --> 00:07:35.689
"You better brace yourself, girl, because
everything has a price.

00:07:35.689 --> 00:07:37.550
That's how witchcraft works."

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:38.770
"But I don't think there's a price for me."

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.770
"Huh?"

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:40.770
"Not anymore."

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.610
"You are racking up a cosmic debt the like
of which the world's never seen."

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:48.089
Owning up to the problem, both Sabrinas agree
to a risky merge procedure that will cause

00:07:48.089 --> 00:07:52.539
at least one of them to lose their memories
and identity, a neat call-back to when Sabrina

00:07:52.539 --> 00:07:55.490
intercepted herself at the end of Part 3.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:57.819
"Shouldn't we merge or something?"

00:07:57.819 --> 00:08:01.229
"Ambrose would say so, yes, but I have a supes
crazy idea."

00:08:01.229 --> 00:08:05.779
I like the way this scene is framed, with
the twins lying next to each other on a stone

00:08:05.779 --> 00:08:09.380
slab, with Sabrina Morningstar on the left
and Spellman on the right,

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:13.839
referencing the dream that Sabrina had in
the very first episode of Season 1 when she

00:08:13.839 --> 00:08:18.780
came across a pair of baby twins on a large
stone in the woods, and the baby on the left

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:21.029
had hooved feet like the Devil.

00:08:21.029 --> 00:08:26.490
And although that merge is abandoned, in a
sense both Sabrinas do end up merged in the

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:30.830
end when Spellman's soul is transferred into
Morningstar's body.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:34.269
Because the series was cancelled after filming
for Part 4 had been completed,

00:08:34.269 --> 00:08:38.530
there are some big plot points and character
arcs that were left wide open to explore in

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.539
what would have been the next season.

00:08:40.539 --> 00:08:45.300
Lilith had an especially traumatic time in
Part 4, with Caliban first cursing her pregnant

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:49.680
belly to explode which almost killed her,
and then Lucifer threatening to take away

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:50.680
her son.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:54.600
"As Romulus and Remus suckled on the teat
of a wolf, so our son shall suckle on the

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.509
teat of a hellhound.

00:08:56.509 --> 00:08:58.949
You have six last hours to spend with Adam."

00:08:58.949 --> 00:09:04.300
In a desperate act, rather than hand her baby
over to the Dark Lord, she kills him and serves

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:07.509
him as a meal,
which also serves as revenge for when Lucifer

00:09:07.509 --> 00:09:12.779
killed Mary Wardwell's fiancé Adam in the
second season and cooked him as a dinner for

00:09:12.779 --> 00:09:13.779
Lilith.

00:09:13.779 --> 00:09:17.319
Enraged, Lucifer strips Lilith of her powers
and inflicts her with human weakness but the

00:09:17.319 --> 00:09:18.589
inability to die.

00:09:18.589 --> 00:09:22.860
So, she asks Caliban to get her the Spear
of Longinus so she can kill herself;

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:28.279
but after Zelda convinces her not to throw
her life away, she uses it to stab Lucifer

00:09:28.279 --> 00:09:31.680
after he reneges on a deal to restore her
abilities.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:36.740
It's a gruesome but powerful moment when she
consumes his celestial blood and powers.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:41.110
With Lucifer cast out of Hell and Caliban
stuck in the Void, the season ends with Madame

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:45.310
Satan back in charge of the infernal realm,
and it would have been fascinating to see

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:48.360
what she would have got up to in Part 5.

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:53.680
The series' long-running villain Father Blackwood
is finally defeated by the very end, as Prudence

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:57.550
chops him up into tiny pieces to scatter across
the world.

00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:02.250
Even with his immortality, it would be highly
unlikely he'd ever re-form his body again.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:06.970
However, continuing his work is Ms Wardwell
who we see reading the Eldritch Gospel to

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:11.350
the Pilgrims of the Night Church and recounting
the events of the final episode.

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:15.060
So a fifth season could have brought her back
as a potential antagonist.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:20.520
There were also numerous pointers to a war
brewing throughout Part 4, with a few scenes

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:24.660
showing that the denizens of Hell were unhappy
with the Greendale coven's worship of the

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:25.850
goddess Hecate.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:31.000
"The witches are without the Dark Lord's gifts.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.949
They now worship Hecate.

00:10:32.949 --> 00:10:34.410
They mean war."

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:41.470
And we know from showrunner Roberto Aguirre-Sacasa
that Part 5 was originally going to deal with

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:43.420
what he called a "Witch War".

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:48.769
I also expect that originally Sabrina's death
in Part 4 wasn't going to be permanent and

00:10:48.769 --> 00:10:50.420
would have been reversed in some way.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:54.920
In fact, there's a line that Zelda says to
Hilda after burying both the Sabrinas that

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.300
seems to hint at this.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.670
"Why did you not preserve her, Dark Mother?

00:10:58.670 --> 00:10:59.959
It's not right, Hilda.

00:10:59.959 --> 00:11:01.940
It's just not right that she's gone."

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:06.790
Zelda is referring to Hecate, and how they
all prayed to her during Sabrina's bloodletting

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.279
to keep her alive.

00:11:08.279 --> 00:11:12.649
We've already seen how Hecate has been able
to bring the dead back to life in the series,

00:11:12.649 --> 00:11:16.740
for instance Hilda in Part 3,
which makes me wonder whether there was originally

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:20.899
an alternate ending that at least hinted at
Sabrina's return?

00:11:20.899 --> 00:11:24.960
Perhaps the original final scene was just
a flicker of life from Sabrina's grave, à

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:27.100
la Batman v Superman?

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:30.360
Or whether that would have just been seen
at the start of Part 5?

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:35.250
Of course, in a supernatural world like CAOS
anything can happen, and even the showrunner

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:38.990
has hinted that there could be something still
to come after Part 4,

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:43.339
although whether this is just the promised
comic book follow-up or a spin-off, prequel,

00:11:43.339 --> 00:11:46.129
or crossover in Riverdale remains to be seen.

00:11:46.129 --> 00:11:50.040
And if you haven't had enough Sabrina yet,
you can discover more of the amazing details

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:54.459
and easter eggs cleverly hidden in the show
in my CAOS Things You Missed video.

00:11:54.459 --> 00:11:57.500
Tap here to watch that or follow the link
in the video description.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:02.149
So, what were your thoughts on the fourth
and final season of Chilling Adventures?

00:12:02.149 --> 00:12:05.649
Were you happy with the ending or what else
would you have liked to see?

00:12:05.649 --> 00:12:07.100
Leave your comments below!

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:10.850
And if you enjoyed this, don't forget to leave
a thumbs-up, it's hugely appreciated.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:15.450
Now tap left for my next Sabrina video or
tap right for something else you're sure to

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:16.450
like.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:18.110
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:19.189
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

